WEBVTT

NOTE Cues sit near the top (line:4%) so they don't cover on-screen labels.

1a-1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.299 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC began as a capstone project in Columbia

1a-2
00:00:03.299 --> 00:00:05.367 line:4% align:center
University’s Master of Science in

1a-3
00:00:05.367 --> 00:00:07.862 line:4% align:center
Sustainability Management program, with a

1a-4
00:00:07.862 --> 00:00:09.200 line:4% align:center
simple-sounding brief:

1b-1
00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.542 line:4% align:center
build a global sustainability rating system

1b-2
00:00:12.542 --> 00:00:14.600 line:4% align:center
for small and medium enterprises.

2a-1
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.530 line:4% align:center
But what should a global rating measure?

2b-1
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:21.770 line:4% align:center
A business can face international frameworks,

2b-2
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:23.763 line:4% align:center
buyer questionnaires and local

2b-3
00:00:23.763 --> 00:00:25.490 line:4% align:center
expectations, all at once.

2c-1
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.099 line:4% align:center
They don't use the same words, ask for the

2c-2
00:00:28.099 --> 00:00:30.910 line:4% align:center
same evidence, or weigh the same issues equally.

3a-1
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.103 line:4% align:center
One universal checklist would miss what makes

3a-2
00:00:34.103 --> 00:00:35.470 line:4% align:center
each business different.

4a-1
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:38.570 line:4% align:center
So the team built a different kind of system.

4b-1
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:41.623 line:4% align:center
First, standards are broken into individual

4b-2
00:00:41.623 --> 00:00:44.410 line:4% align:center
requirements, each traced back to its source.

4c-1
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:47.566 line:4% align:center
Next, the business's context decides which

4c-2
00:00:47.566 --> 00:00:50.180 line:4% align:center
questions apply, and which matter more.

4d-1
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.074 line:4% align:center
Then fixed rules calculate the scores, the

4d-2
00:00:53.074 --> 00:00:54.890 line:4% align:center
same way for every business.

4e-1
00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:56.995 line:4% align:center
AI has two bounded jobs:

4e-2
00:00:56.995 --> 00:00:59.308 line:4% align:center
helping prepare the sources, and

4e-3
00:00:59.308 --> 00:01:00.970 line:4% align:center
explaining the results.

5a-1
00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.892 line:4% align:center
Because the method is separate from its

5a-2
00:01:03.892 --> 00:01:06.233 line:4% align:center
sources, it could be configured for any set

5a-3
00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:06.940 line:4% align:center
of standards.

5b-1
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:10.643 line:4% align:center
A large buyer or an industry association could

5b-2
00:01:10.643 --> 00:01:12.653 line:4% align:center
generate its own assessment:

5b-3
00:01:12.653 --> 00:01:15.956 line:4% align:center
questions, weights and scoring, built from the

5b-4
00:01:15.956 --> 00:01:18.110 line:4% align:center
standards it cares about most.

6a-1
00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.700 line:4% align:center
MOSAIC. The pieces that matter.
